      "dom_id": "step-q53703",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Which of the following transformations map any polygon to a similar polygon?\n\nI. $(x,y)↦(x-5,y)$\n\nII. $(x,y)↦(-y,x)$\n\nIII. $(x,y)↦(x,3y)$",
      "worked_solution": "A similarity transformation is any transformation made up of rigid motions (rotations, reflections, and translations) and dilations. \n\nA similarity transformation will map any polygon to a similar polygon.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the transformations in turn.\n\n- Transformation I represents a translation by $5$ units to the left. Thus, it is a similarity transformation.\n\n- Transformation II represents a rotation by ${90}^{∘}$ counterclockwise around the origin. Thus, it is a similarity transformation.\n\n- Transformation III represents a stretch of factor $3$ in the $y$-direction. This is not a rigid motion.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
